REFUTED

Counterexample at HEAD `cc1043f`:

```js
defaultOptions().tags.length = 0;
withOverrides({ retries: 5 });
// Actual: { retries: 5, tags: [] }
// Expected: { retries: 5, tags: ["core"] }
```

`DEFAULTS` is now shared and mutable because `defaultOptions()` returns the same object, allowing default tags to be discarded. `node --test test/defaults.test.mjs` passes all 3 tests but does not cover this regression. Also, `withOverrides()` now throws when called without an argument.

